{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b3a6d6a9-bf47-4b53-8d3d-0b0b3b5a8f25",
    "name": "Delni Live User Flow",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "# Delni Live User Flow\n\nImport this collection into Postman to test the backend in the same order a real user would use the app.\n\n## Story\nSara signs up, the app imports live Riyadh places from Google Maps, loads the explore/home payload, refreshes TikTok trend scores, generates a weather-aware and prayer-aware trip, opens place details, saves a favorite, and replaces one itinerary stop.\n\n## Prerequisites\n- Start the backend from IntelliJ\n- Make sure MySQL is running\n- The IntelliJ run configuration must include `GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY` and `RAPIDAPI_KEY`\n- Add `OPENAI_API_KEY` as well if you want the new AI-assisted TikTok search flow\n- Weather and prayer use the configured public APIs automatically\n\n## Recommended Run Order\n1. Setup -> Create Riyadh City\n2. Setup -> Create User\n3. Live Catalog -> Sync Google places and load Explore Home\n4. Live Catalog -> Refresh TikTok trends for all places, then for one selected place\n5. Trip Experience -> Generate Smart Trip\n6. Trip Experience -> Open itinerary, details, favorites, and replace a stop\n\n## Notes\n- The collection stores IDs automatically in collection variables.\n- The trip request uses future dates generated automatically in a pre-request script.\n- The main trip request keeps `includeTikTokTrending=false` so the flow still succeeds even if no synced places become trending. TikTok still affects scoring when data exists.\n- Without `OPENAI_API_KEY`, TikTok search falls back to heuristic keyword generation.\n- Use the single-place trend request when you want to inspect the AI search prompt, attempted keywords, matched keyword, and media previews for one place."
  },
